  "notes": "The Firebliss Patera: a lava lake 48 x 32 km under a thin black crust, in the Great Firebliss Vale's old floor, its crust at 2,240 m behind walls of 2.7-4.5 km. Once a year the crust founders: two fronts start at the west shore and run round both sides of the Holm at about a kilometre a day, meeting on the east shore some 40-60 days later. About 3-4 TW: a permanent heat low, its storm column over the lake and a ring of rain and lightning round it. biomes/firebliss/PLAN.md section 1a; the owner, 2026-11-12."
